WEBVTT

00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:04.540
Energy-smart workflows make important work less dependent on perfect willpower.

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.115
Time blocking by energy level is one practical move.

00:00:07.115 --> 00:00:09.120
Put deep work, difficult decisions, learning,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.680
and creative problem solving into better capacity windows when possible.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:15.160
Put lower-intensity administration into batches.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.025
This reduces the number of times attention has to shift and helps protect the kind of

00:00:19.025 --> 00:00:20.700
energy each task requires.

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:22.774
Meeting hygiene is part of workflow design.

00:00:22.774 --> 00:00:25.950
Meetings should have a purpose, the right participants, a realistic scope,

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.310
and a useful outcome.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.520
Decision batching can reduce the number of scattered choices across the day.

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.275
Checklists can lower cognitive load for recurring tasks.

00:00:33.275 --> 00:00:37.345
Templates and defaults reduce startup cost because people do not have to recreate the same

00:00:37.345 --> 00:00:38.619
structure every time.

00:00:38.619 --> 00:00:39.940
Shutdown routines help close loops.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.570
A useful shutdown can capture unfinished work, identify the next action, record decisions,

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.435
and clear enough mental space to stop carrying the day forward.

00:00:47.435 --> 00:00:49.136
This is not about forcing longer workdays.

00:00:49.136 --> 00:00:53.530
It is about making the next start easier and reducing the background hum of unresolved

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.280
commitments.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.469
A clean stop often creates a cleaner start.

00:00:56.469 --> 00:00:57.810
Distraction design matters too.

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.880
Create friction for distractions and reduce friction for important work.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:03.850
That might mean turning off nonessential alerts during focus blocks,

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:06.450
keeping key materials ready, using a visible task limit,

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:08.600
or setting a default place for decisions.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.040
The best workflow is not the most elaborate system.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.840
It is the system that quietly makes the right action easier under real conditions.
